{
  "$schema": "./icons.schema.json",
  "description": "EXP-273 — the single icon registry for web, iOS, Android and desktop. Every value is a Lucide icon name as shipped by lucide-react (the version in apps/web/package.json); the generator reads that package's `__iconNode` geometry, so all four clients render byte-identical art. `pickable` is the user-facing icon set (board icon picker + action icon picker) and MUST stay byte-equal to contract.json's boardIcon.values — append only, never reorder or remove, or stored boards.icon values are orphaned. `semantic` maps a stable concept id to a Lucide name so re-pointing an icon is a one-line edit here. `custom` (EXP-314) holds hand-authored glyphs Lucide does not ship — same IconNode geometry format as lucide's `__iconNode`, flowing through the identical 4-platform emit; names must not collide with a Lucide icon or a hand-maintained desktop brand mark, and glyphs must stay single-color (desktop rasterizes SVGs to a one-tint alpha mask). EXP-317: a concept only unifies the clients that RESOLVE through it — every cross-client surface must name one (`conceptIcon()` on web, `registry::CONST` on desktop, `AppIcons.`/`ExpIcons.` on iOS/Android) instead of importing a glyph directly, and `apps/web/src/lib/icons.test.ts` gates the three ways that used to slip: settings-nav concept parity between web and desktop, gpui-component `IconName` on desktop, and deprecated lucide aliases on web.",
